%% Phase 2: Design and review (autonomous, no Owner)
%%
%% Agents never talk to each other. Each one picks up an artifact in a state it handles,
%% writes its result onto the artifact, and moves the artifact to the next state.
%% In Samba the orchestrator does the polling and runs one fresh agent per item.
%%
%% TEP states:
%%   draft -> in-review -> approved
%%                      -> changes-requested -> in-review   (loop, capped)
%%                      -> blocked            (round cap, or contradicts an accepted ADR)
%%   approved -> amend -> in-review                         (a task found the TEP wrong)
%% Epic states touched: ready -> designing -> designed
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  box Agents
    participant Des as Designer
    participant Rev as Reviewer
  end

  box Artifacts
    participant Epics@{ "type" : "collections" }
    participant TEPs@{ "type" : "collections" }
    participant Backlog@{ "type" : "collections" }
    participant Questions@{ "type" : "collections" }
  end

  Des->>Epics: pick up an Epic in state ready
  Epics->>Des: the Epic. Epic becomes designing
  Des->>Des: reads Epic, ADRs, spec, code
  Des->>TEPs: write TEP in state draft (interfaces, order, invariants, file list)
  TEPs->>TEPs: draft becomes in-review

  Rev->>TEPs: pick up a TEP in state in-review
  TEPs->>Rev: the TEP
  Rev->>Rev: fresh context, reads TEP, Epic, ADRs, spec, code
  Note over Rev: Architect lens and Senior Developer lens, one call, two sections

  alt Blocker or Major findings
    Rev->>TEPs: write findings on the TEP. State becomes changes-requested
    Des->>TEPs: pick up a TEP in state changes-requested
    Des->>TEPs: fix, or contest with evidence the Reviewer could read. State becomes in-review
    Note over Des,Rev: loop, with a round cap. Settled findings stay settled
  else TEP contradicts an accepted ADR, or round cap reached
    Rev->>TEPs: state becomes blocked
    Rev->>Questions: ask the Owner (supersede the ADR, or fix the TEP?)
  else only Nits, or no findings
    Rev->>TEPs: write the review report (nits, ADR candidates). State becomes approved
    Rev->>Epics: Epic becomes designed
    Rev->>Backlog: nits and ADR candidates become backlog items in state open
  end

  Note over Des,TEPs: Amendment path, triggered from implementation
  Des->>TEPs: pick up a TEP in state amend
  Des->>TEPs: revise the TEP. State becomes in-review
